WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.407
I'm Mike Sadowski, with Chet's Cleaning,

00:00:14.407 --> 00:00:16.920
and we are out of Madison
Heights, Michigan,

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.870
and we clean just about everything

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.280
except for walls and windows.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.730
Today we're going to be
cleaning a dirty boat cover.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.900
The simple reason for the boat cover

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.760
is just to keep the inside of the boat

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.950
not looking like the cover did.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.560
So that way, the cover takes
the brunt of the elements

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.913
rather than the boat.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.410
The material of the boat
cover is a Sunbrella material.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.210
It's a solution-dyed acrylic,

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.460
so it has great stain-resist properties

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.110
and it's pretty friendly for the sun,

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.970
which is how it can survive out there.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:51.660
This one was primarily
animal issues flying overhead

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.120
and some mold that was built up from use.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.520
I would guess it was
probably about five years

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.011
out in the elements.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.310
The chemicals that we
use, it's called DOT.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.700
There's dichlor granules in
there, which is a chlorine,

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.590
and then there is a surfactant,

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.390
so a detergent in there, which allows us

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:18.240
to get the soil off along
with the mold and mildew.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.020
DOT is very chemical-friendly, in terms of

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:22.890
it's not going to burn my skin at all.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.600
It's virtually odorless.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.210
We use dwell time to allow the solution

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.385
to break down any of the soils, mold,

00:01:29.385 --> 00:01:30.900
mildew that's in there.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.460
Needs at least a half an hour,

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.991
but I can let it sit overnight at times.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.450
Once that's had time to
do what it needs to do,

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.340
we go ahead and use agitation.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.010
So a scrub brush, either
by hand or mechanical.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.230
The yellow machine, it's called a Cimex.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.771
It's an orbital scrubber,

00:01:47.771 --> 00:01:49.404
so the scrub pads at the bottom

00:01:49.404 --> 00:01:51.300
are just going in a circular motion

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.400
while the head turns in
a different direction.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.430
What it's doing is pulling
apart the fibers slightly,

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.350
the way they're woven, and it allows

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.720
the soil and embedded mold and mildew

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.280
to release a little bit easier

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.272
rather than still being
tightly woven with the fibers.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.520
The high-pressure water is
what really breaks apart

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.840
everything that's down in there.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.450
It's a mild detergent
that we use in rug washing

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.880
that is going through
the power-washing gun.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.980
So, it's not just water,
it's soap and water

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.380
coming out at the same time.

00:02:25.799 --> 00:02:29.374
I'm using the broom to push
water off of the boat cover.

00:02:29.374 --> 00:02:32.100
A lot of times, whether
it's the boat cover or rugs,

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.830
it's very hard to see
staining that's remaining

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.570
when the water's puddled on there,

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.680
so I'm just pushing it off,

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.510
so that way I'm able
to see what's going on

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.280
and make sure that I didn't miss any areas

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.933
while I was power washing.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.450
The bath that it goes into,

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.275
I was just using it to help rinse out

00:02:50.275 --> 00:02:52.125
all of the detergent and the products

00:02:52.125 --> 00:02:54.000
that I had put onto the boat cover,

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.553
because whatever I use I
want to make sure I get off.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.057
I put it through our rinse wringer.

00:03:01.057 --> 00:03:03.390
So that was just squeegeeing
out some of the water

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:05.580
and hitting it with another
high-pressure system

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.860
to get another power-washing
job going through,

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.260
and making sure I was getting
it as clean as possible.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.150
From there, we went ahead
and hung it and dried it.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.370
With boat covers, I
typically don't get them

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:18.870
when they look clean,
where rugs and upholstery,

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.150
I would tell you it should
be cleaned regularly

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:23.130
no matter what the appearance.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.020
Boat covers I go a little bit different.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.940
They are cleaned as needed.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.672
If it gets real bad and you want it clean,

00:03:28.672 --> 00:03:30.847
that would be the time.
If it's a generic cover,

00:03:30.847 --> 00:03:32.550
it might not even be worth cleaning.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.010
You just let it live
its life and replace it.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:37.080
Other times they might
outweigh the benefit

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.360
of trying to find material
and get a new one made,

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.000
and just have it cleaned up,
buy them a few more years.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.496
The biggest thing that I've ran into,

00:03:44.496 --> 00:03:47.880
whether it's from sun damage
or aggressive cleaning,

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:49.571
you actually cause that Sunbrella

00:03:49.571 --> 00:03:51.296
to not become as repellent.

00:03:51.296 --> 00:03:54.330
And Sunbrella does sell
a product to reapply

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.430
that repellency, or the protectant, to it.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.500
So, depending on the scenario,

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.180
people want to look to get that done also

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.238
to make sure it stays in good shape.

